DO NOT DO:
  - Do not reach for `linkme` or `inventory` for the story registry. Both were
    tested and both fail on wasm. See LOG-0002 / S2 before revisiting.
  - Do not pass `--hot-patch` to dx serve. It does not build.
  - Do not split the manager and preview into two CRATES/BUNDLES. It was the
    plan and it is worse: two builds, a hand-written iframe.html, and a manager
    that can no longer see the registry it needs for the sidebar and the props
    tables. One bundle loaded twice gives the same isolation. LOG-0005 / F1.
  - Do not add a `_ =>` wildcard arm to `wire::encode`. `Event` is
    #[non_exhaustive] for downstream crates but exhaustive inside core, so a new
    variant FAILS TO COMPILE until it is given a wire form. That is the only
    thing stopping a new message from silently going nowhere.
  - Do not put a global's DEFAULT on the wire or in the URL. Only selections
    travel; both halves fill in the declarations themselves, which they can
    because the declarations are &'static and both halves share the bundle. It
    is also what makes "the selection map is empty" mean "nothing is changed",
    which is the question the reset button asks. LOG-0006 / G3.
  - Do not compare a global (or an arg, or a viewport name) straight out of a
    URL against a typed ArgValue. The query-string codec is UNTYPED by design:
    `theme:dark` decodes as Text, never Variant. Coerce first. LOG-0006 / G2.
  - Do not invent a fourth value vocabulary. args change per story, parameters
    are static per level, globals change for the whole book. The viewport addon
    is the worked example of staying inside those three — and the reason its
    available LIST is a Project declaration rather than a parameter is precisely
    that ParamValue cannot hold a record. LOG-0006 / G1, LOG-0007 / F2.
  - Do not make the iframe's `src` track live state. Changing `src` reloads the
    frame; it is computed once at mount, and only the reload button touches it.
    The viewport changes the frame's STYLE for the same reason. LOG-0007 / F1.
  - Do not let either half act on its own messages. InProcessChannel broadcasts
    to the emitter too; postMessage does not. tests/two_documents.rs holds the
    line — its harness deliberately has the stricter behaviour. This also means
    a test that injects SetCurrentStory moves the PREVIEW only; to test the
    shell landing somewhere, change the order of the story slice.
  - Do not let the MANAGER call StoryDef::base_args() or render a decorator.
    Both need a live scope and a story, and the manager has neither. The manager
    is given the Project for TWO reasons now: the globals the toolbar offers,
    and the viewports the picker offers. Reading a story's PARAMETERS is fine —
    they are static data, and the manager needs them to size the frame.
  - Do not render a story body inline in the preview again. Stories get their
    own scope via StoryHost, remounted per story. See LOG-0004 / F2.
  - Do not "simplify" the one-element `for def in [def]` loop around StoryHost
    into a plain child. Dioxus only honours `key` when diffing a LIST; a lone
    keyed child is re-rendered in place and the hook bug comes back. Note the
    flip side: StoryHost is keyed on the STORY ID, so changing a global
    re-renders it in place and a story's hook state survives. That is wanted.
  - Do not add a controls panel that mutates the preview's args signal directly.
    Route it through the Channel.
  - Do not emit a `macro_rules!` from one proc macro for another to call with a
    value argument. It compiles and it breaks rust-analyzer. See standing facts.
  - Do not construct StoryDef/Meta with struct literals. Fields are private on
    purpose; use the const builders so adding a field stays non-breaking.
  - Do not derive Default on a config struct whose `const fn new()` is no longer
    all-zeroes. Project::new() fills in DEFAULT_VIEWPORTS, so a derived Default
    would have given `#[props(default)]` a different project. LOG-0007 / F5.
  - Do not put ArgType on the wire. It holds &'static str; the manager reads the
    const table directly instead — which works because it shares the bundle.
  - Do not create a signal in a CHILD scope that an ANCESTOR's code writes. The
    channel listener runs in the emitter's scope, so preview signals written by
    the manager must be Signal::new_in_scope(.., ScopeId::ROOT). See LOG-0004/F8.
  - Do not trust a green suite for UI work. 92 tests passed while two real
    defects sat in the running app; 152 passed while the toolbar's dropdowns
    were unusable from the keyboard. Open the browser and click it.
  - Do not emit `<label for=..>` unconditionally in the controls panel. Action
    and skipped rows render prose with no control to point at, and radio rows
    key their inputs per option. Use `label_target`. See LOG-0004/F9.


